<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-138] Ensure that utility cache is really executed in utility pool</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-138</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;See GridCacheIoManager:&lt;br/&gt;
1) sendOrderedMessaage() always use system pool.&lt;br/&gt;
2) safeSend() always use system pool.&lt;br/&gt;
3) send(ClusterNode, GridCacheMessage) use system pool implicitly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;With such design there is a great risk that system cache either already process some of it&apos;s messages in system pool instead of utility pool, or will do it at some point in future.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Possible solutions:&lt;br/&gt;
1) Move GridCacheIoManager from shared context to cache context.&lt;br/&gt;
2) Force all public methods to specify IO policy explicitly.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
